# SABOTAGE: T166 / ADR-050 §4.6 — the public page's slug MASK is defeated twice
# over: the bounded operator shape is widened to admit `_` and capitals, and the
# explicit `vt_` refusal beside it is deleted. `slug` is the only string that
# crosses to the public plane, and ADR-044 §5.2's guarantee that it is
# operator-typed cockpit-side is a CONVENTION about who writes the column, not a
# constraint the column enforces — which is exactly why the renderer refuses
# anything outside the shape instead of trusting it. With both guards gone a value
# that reached the slug column renders verbatim: a `vt_*` vault token, a tenant's
# legal name, an operator's e-mail address.
#
# Flips the named §4.6 red (the `vt_`-shaped smuggled value must render `••••`).
# Everything else stays GREEN: the opt-in filter, the internal→public enum mapping,
# the deregistered exclusion and the `Entry` two-field closure all still hold, and
# the mask's own POSITIVE CONTROL (a slug that IS the bounded shape renders
# unmasked) still passes — so the red fails because the mask was widened, not
# because slugs stopped rendering.
#
# NOT TOUCHED, deliberately: `@masked` itself and the non-binary `public_slug/1`
# clause (both still reached, so no clause goes dead and no attribute goes unused
# under `--warnings-as-errors`), the status mapping, and the web layer's HTML
# escaping — escaping is not masking, and a token is just as leaked escaped.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/fleet_public_status_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: a vt_-shaped value smuggled into the slug renders
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/fleet/public_status.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/fleet/public_status.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/fleet/public_status.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/fleet/public_status.ex
@@ -90,7 +90,9 @@ defmodule Samen.Fleet.PublicStatus do
   # The bounded operator slug shape (ADR-044 §5.2). Anchored, length-capped,
   # lowercase-and-dash only: no `_` (so every `vt_*` token fails it), no `@`, no
   # whitespace, no capitals.
-  @slug_shape ~r/\A[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,62}\z/
+  # SABOTAGE (T166/ADR-050 §4.6): the bounded operator shape is WIDENED to admit
+  # `_` and capitals, which is exactly the class `vt_*` lives in.
+  @slug_shape ~r/\A[a-zA-Z0-9][a-zA-Z0-9_-]{0,62}\z/
 
   @type view :: %{entries: [Entry.t()], overall: atom()}
 
@@ -173,7 +175,9 @@ defmodule Samen.Fleet.PublicStatus do
   defp public_status(_other), do: :down
 
   defp public_slug(slug) when is_binary(slug) do
-    if Regex.match?(@slug_shape, slug) and not String.starts_with?(slug, "vt_") do
+    # SABOTAGE (T166/ADR-050 §4.6): the explicit `vt_` refusal is deleted too, so a
+    # vault token in the slug column renders verbatim on the public page.
+    if Regex.match?(@slug_shape, slug) do
       slug
     else
       @masked
